WEBVTT

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.900
<i>GeGeGe no Kitaro</i>

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.530
Dad, help!

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:28.450
Dad!

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:38.290
<i>The world you see isn't all there is.</i>

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.130
<i>There are things you can't see.</i>

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:44.970
<i>See? In the darkness behind you...</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:04.860
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>Slumbering in bed in the morning</i>

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.780
<i>asa wa nedoko de gu gu gu</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.500
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>Ghosts don't have school</i>

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:17.290
<i>obakenya gakkou mo</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>Or tests or anything</i>

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.170
<i>shiken mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:25.970
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:29.550
<i>minna de utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:33.770
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>Sports festivals in the graveyard at night</i>

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.640
<i>yoru wa hakaba de undoukai</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>It's so fun, it's so fun</i>

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.520
<i>tanoshiina tanoshiina</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>Ghosts don't die</i>

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:46.650
<i>obake wa shinanai</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>Or get sick or anything</i>

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.070
<i>byouki mo nannimo nai</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>Ge, ge, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:54.540
<i>ge ge gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:58.870
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.840
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>Let's all sing together, gegege no ge</i>

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:07.800
<i>minnade utaou gegege no ge</i>

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:12.470
Dad!

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.200
Dad!

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:19.520
Dad, it's me, Masashi!
I know you're in there!

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.440
Dad...

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:38.980
Dad.

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:42.040
Wait up, everybody.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.860
Dad, come on! Wake up!

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:49.680
Dad!

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.240
Dad...!

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:59.430
No one's been able to reach you
for two weeks! Everyone's worried!

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.440
Why did you wake me?

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:08.970
D-Dad...

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:13.680
Why'd you wake me... Why'd you wake me...

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:17.260
Why?!

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:23.830
CHAPTER 14

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:28.860
MAKURA-GAESHI AND THE FANTASTIC DREAM

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:30.860
Huh? Fired?

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.620
By fired, you mean... Huh?

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:38.120
Uchida-san, I've given you numerous
chances to make up for your mistakes.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.170
I can't cover for you anymore.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.000
W-Wait a minute.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.460
If I lose my job now
my wife will never come back!

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.610
You have my sympathies.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.510
But...

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.850
-Let's check it out some time.
-Sure!

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:54.810
<i>Why are you calling me now?</i>

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:57.010
Well, actually...

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.560
Oh, how's Masashi doing?

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:03.270
<i>Fine. He helps out and is studying hard.</i>

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:07.420
<i>You know, I think not having you around
is better for his growth.</i>

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.900
I-I see...

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.780
<i>What do you want? I'm busy.</i>

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:16.010
Oh, it's nothing.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:20.080
RECRUITMENT SITE

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:37.050
<i>"We regret to inform
you have not be selected..."</i>

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.850
Dammit...

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:07.440
Masashi, I'm sorry.
It looks like your dad's finished...

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:23.060
<i>Kagome, kagome</i>

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:26.860
<i>The bird inside the cage</i>

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:30.480
<i>When oh when will it come out?</i>

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:34.280
<i>In the night of dawn</i>

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:37.700
<i>A crane and a turtle slipped and fell</i>

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:39.570
H-Hey, you kids.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:41.830
<i>The person behind you</i>

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:44.200
Who is it?

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:51.170
K-kids, what time do you think it is?
Go home already.

00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:55.300
Why do you say things
that a grown-up would?

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.590
Because I'm a grown-up.

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:01.060
I have a son about your age.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.010
So I was just worried.

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:04.290
Liar.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:07.350
You're just a kid.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:08.370
Huh?

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:10.540
But...

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:13.590
Come on. Let's go.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:22.830
Come.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:39.380
Mana mentioned it the other day, but...

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:42.640
Daddy Eyeball-san,
you don't look like Kitaro at all.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:45.350
You're really his father, right?

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:46.810
Of course.

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:51.060
I'm just the eyeball that remains
from my former body.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:53.900
Huh? So you used to have a normal body?

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:56.610
What, you didn't know, Catchick?

00:06:56.610 --> 00:07:00.950
Daddy Eyeball may look this way now,
but when he was younger

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:05.370
he was the young descendent of
the Ghost Tribe and quite handsome, too.

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:06.910
Oh really?

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:08.870
You didn't know either, Kitaro?

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:12.370
I wish I could've met you back then, Dad.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:16.020
It's in the past now.

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:20.220
Hey guys, there's a letter in the mailbox.

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:25.010
Your father nearly killed you?

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:34.780
He fell back to sleep almost immediately,
so he never hit me, though.

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:36.320
Oh my...

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:40.320
But now he won't wake up anymore.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:46.700
When I mentioned it to Inuyama-san,
she said you'd help, Kitaro-san...

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:49.000
There are rumors on the web, too.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:52.840
They say lots of other grown-ups
are asleep and won't wake up.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:57.770
Dad's always so kind to me.
I can't believe he'd try to kill me...

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:04.870
Masashi-kun, a father would never do
something like that to a child he loves!

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:10.190
He must be under someone's control.

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.160
What?

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:17.070
Your father won't wake up because
his soul must be stuck in the Dream World.

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:20.210
In that case,
that guy must know something.

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:21.570
That guy?

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:24.070
The Makura-Gaeshi!

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:26.200
I don't know about that!

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:28.910
MAKURA-GAESHI

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:35.170
You tried to kidnap children to the Dream
World and eat them once, didn't you?

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:40.590
Ever since some scary monk beat me up
I haven't done that.

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:42.460
I swear on this pillow!

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:46.140
Is that all? Good night.

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:50.760
Oh. What a letdown.

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:52.520
What?!

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:54.000
Hey, Mana!

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:59.030
I was told that Makura-Gaeshi is
an amazing guy who knows all about dreams,

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:01.030
but he doesn't know anything.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:03.410
Hey! What did you say?!

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:07.660
He should just admit that since
he doesn't know he can't do anything.

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:11.500
I'm the <i>yokai</i> who knows
the most about dreams!

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:13.500
Are you sure?

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:14.880
Just watch!

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.150
<i>Nemu, nemu, nemu, nemu...</i>

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:22.300
Wow, it's a rainbow bridge!

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:28.180
Impressive, huh? Cross this rainbow bridge
and you can go to the Dream World!

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:30.600
Oh wow! Not bad!

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:36.580
Good job motivating him
to help, Mana-chan!

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:39.040
I gotta warn you first.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:45.030
We're all about to barge into a dream
that normally only one person's seeing.

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:49.240
You do that and that Dream World
becomes really unstable.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:50.370
Unstable?

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:54.870
Right. The Dream World is a place
where any crazy dream comes true.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:55.960
Hmm.

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:58.000
So, listen, whatever you do...

00:09:58.350 --> 00:10:00.750
"What if we get attacked by a monster?!"

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:04.470
is the type of thing
you should never think.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:05.300
Huh?!

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:06.760
You two didn't...!

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:14.580
Everybody run!

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:17.270
Why'd you have to think it?!

00:10:17.270 --> 00:10:20.070
Listen!
Definitely don't think that anymore!

00:10:20.070 --> 00:10:22.570
"What if this bridge collapses?!"

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:24.650
is an absolute no-no too!

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:25.530
Huh?!

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:26.570
You didn't...

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:29.680
You had to open your big mouth!

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:31.260
Oh! My bad!

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:37.500
Masashi-kun!

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:38.940
Kitaro-san!

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:47.130
FUDATEN SHRINE (CHOFU CITY)

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:51.640
<i>YOKAI</i> MAKURA-GAESHI

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:51.570
<i>-"Ge."
-"What?"</i>

00:10:56.470 --> 00:10:59.100
<i>Are you all right, Catchick?</i>

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:00.110
<i>Kitaro?!</i>

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:02.860
<i>Glad you're all right! Let's get married!</i>

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:05.860
<i>Huh?</i>

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:07.880
<i>What?!</i>

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.240
<i>Can I copy your homework?!</i>

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:12.790
<i>Oh very well. Just this once.</i>

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:13.740
<i>Thanks!</i>

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:16.240
<i>You're always so nice, Kitaro.</i>

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:19.250
<i>Okay, let's take attendance!</i>

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:21.080
<i>Okay!</i>

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:22.210
Ah crap.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:25.420
The girls are stuck in their own dreams.

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:31.030
Makura-Gaeshi, this is the land of dreams
Masashi-kun's father is trapped in, right?

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:36.390
Yeah. It looks like it's made from
several overlapped grown-ups' dreams.

00:11:36.390 --> 00:11:40.040
This is, Dad and the others' dream...

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:56.010
There it goes!

00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:58.540
Oof!

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:00.290
Darn! It got away!

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:01.210
Got it!

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:03.000
Wow, you're good!

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:04.500
Whoops!

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:07.380
Hey, Akinori! Come on already!

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:10.720
Akinori? That's Dad's name.

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:12.650
Hold on a sec!

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:15.760
Is your name Akinori?

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:18.720
Is it, Akinori Uchida?

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:21.520
Yeah, it is.

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:22.850
<i>Dad!</i>

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:26.770
U-Um...

00:12:27.250 --> 00:12:29.400
You're a good painter.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:33.650
Yeah. When I grow up,
I wanna be a painter!

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:34.950
Huh?

00:12:34.950 --> 00:12:38.660
<i>But Dad doesn't paint at all anymore...</i>

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:42.120
Akinori-kun... No, Masashi-kun's father.

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:42.920
Huh?

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:47.080
How long do you intend to keep
hiding in this dream?

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:51.590
You're a father!
How can you forget your own son?!

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:53.430
What are you talking about?

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:57.180
Those kids are all sleeping grown-ups too.

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:58.930
-Makura-Gaeshi.
-Hm?

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:01.640
Can you force them to wake up?

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:04.520
Yeah, but it'll be a little rough.

00:13:05.170 --> 00:13:06.460
Don't!

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:11.450
Everyone's enjoying themselves
as children.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:16.200
Here they can stay as children
in an eternal dream.

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:17.490
Who are you?

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:22.000
Hey! You've got
the Bell of Dream Control!

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.670
I've heard of that.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:29.420
Makura-Gaeshi used that bell
to kidnap children to the Dream World.

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:31.010
Yeah, that's right.

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:34.010
But the monk who beat me took it away!

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:37.930
So this is your doing!

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:42.180
Those people have families
and people waiting for them!

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:44.310
Free everyone from this dream!

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:45.980
No!

00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:50.070
Everyone came to this Dream World
because reality is too painful!

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:53.480
So why do you want to
force them to wake up?!

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:56.800
Reality... is painful?

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:00.830
I won't allow anyone to break this world.

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:03.460
-That's right!
-Get out of here!

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:06.890
Let's work together
and defeat those people!

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.150
I've got this!

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:16.430
Dad!

00:14:16.430 --> 00:14:20.140
Go, Majin Gunner!

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:24.330
Majin Gunner!

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:30.190
What is this?!

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:34.570
The children's dream must have
taken form and come out!

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:37.570
-Do it, Gunner!
-Beat those bad guys!

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:40.200
Gun Punch!

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:42.240
-Masashi-kun, run!
-O-Okay!

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:46.480
Beam!

00:14:50.560 --> 00:14:53.590
Hey, Kitaro!
Do something amazing like that!

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.630
You say that, but...

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:57.170
Hair Needles!

00:14:58.550 --> 00:15:04.010
Are mundane attacks all you can do?
Don't you have any childlike dreams?!

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:07.020
Kitaro!

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:08.600
<i>That's right.</i>

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:12.980
<i>Left in a graveyard alone
right after birth,</i>

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:17.210
<i>you never had the luxury of
having any childlike dreams...</i>

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:20.590
Spirit Hair Chanchanko!

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:22.990
Separate!

00:15:37.780 --> 00:15:39.150
These are...

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:42.260
...your memories?!

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:45.030
<i>May you at least have good dreams...</i>

00:15:58.610 --> 00:16:04.010
You were sacrificed to a river god
to stop a flood...?!

00:16:10.930 --> 00:16:12.230
Kitaro!

00:16:13.600 --> 00:16:16.210
I died before I could grow up!

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:29.930
And after I died, I saw many grown-ups
who had lost their dreams.

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:34.210
That's why I led those grown-ups
to this world.

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:38.570
So they could play with me forever...

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:48.970
You can die forever as a child too!

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:51.370
Kitaro!

00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:53.440
Dad!

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:55.600
Kitaro!

00:16:57.920 --> 00:16:59.400
Kitaro-san!

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:05.090
Oh no!

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:07.930
Dad!

00:17:11.350 --> 00:17:13.350
Dad, help!

00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:14.730
Give it up!

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:17.230
Dad!

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:20.190
Dad...?

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:31.290
This is...

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:38.830
Masashi!

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:47.350
Masashi!

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:49.680
Masashi!!

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:51.600
Impossible!

00:17:59.690 --> 00:18:02.190
Dammit, Makura-Gaeshi,
lend me your power!

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:04.280
-Huh? My power?!
-Kitaro!

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:10.370
Everybody's a damn fool! Dammit!

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:12.470
<i>Nemu, nemu, nemu, nemu...</i>

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:16.660
Kitaro!

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:25.470
I'm sorry, Kitaro.
If I hadn't ended up in this form,

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:29.560
maybe I could have let you lead
a normal childhood.

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:32.140
But, that wasn't possible.

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:36.650
If I could, I would've liked to
have been a father

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:41.420
who could protect you
and let you dream childlike dreams...

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:00.940
You...

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:02.840
Who are you?!

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:08.240
One who'd do anything
to protect his child...

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:13.200
I'm just a father.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:20.100
Kitaro.

00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:33.930
Dreams must end.
That's what makes them precious.

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:37.640
I'm ending this dream!

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:41.540
Finger Guns!

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:15.990
Are you all right, Kitaro?!

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:19.030
Dad. What about Masashi-kun...?

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:20.230
Don't worry.

00:20:20.580 --> 00:20:22.840
Masashi, I'm sorry.

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:26.000
It's okay, Dad. I'm glad you're back.

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:27.110
Yeah.

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:30.380
Thank you.

00:20:30.380 --> 00:20:31.340
Huh?

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:34.900
The Dream World was really fun.

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:37.180
But I can't stay forever.

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:40.220
I'm Masashi's father.

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:43.190
Next time,
I'll dream together with Masashi.

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:44.750
Oh...

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:50.690
The bell is broken,
so I can't freely control it anymore,

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:54.780
but the Dream World will always be here.

00:20:54.780 --> 00:20:58.220
If it ever gets too hard,
feel free to come back.

00:20:58.530 --> 00:21:00.810
I'm never coming back.

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:10.150
I certainly hope so...

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:15.470
Whew. I guess that ends that.

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:19.980
The grown-ups trapped in the dream
are probably waking up by now.

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:22.440
Everyone, thank you very much!

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:24.060
It was nothing!

00:21:24.060 --> 00:21:26.860
You two didn't do a damn thing!

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:29.530
You were both stuck in your silly dreams.

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:31.690
-Oh be quiet!
-Yeah!

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:39.260
Kitaro, I was never able to let you
lead a normal childhood.

00:21:40.010 --> 00:21:41.580
I'm sorry.

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:46.000
It's okay. I know you're always
thinking of me, Dad,

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:49.270
and have always
been there protecting me.

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:52.420
Thank you, Dad.

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:54.670
Kitaro...

00:21:57.740 --> 00:21:58.570
Oh!

00:21:59.530 --> 00:22:01.660
It's a rainbow, Dad!

